  "critical_findings": [
    "The original theory formally covers observation contexts, probes, nested scales/intensity, fingerprints, equivalence/fibers/quotients, probe equivalence, closure, factorization, pair thresholds and boundary status, minimum-double law, derived ultrametric, empirical threshold measure/resolution curve, representation regimes, compatible transitions, trajectories, learned probes, meta-observation, language prediction/action distinction, typed deficits, constraints, provenance/security, constrained search/generation, append-only library, relative transfer, observation-imagination-revision, and bisimulation/pruning.",
    "eLLM_v0 uses suffix probes primarily for diagnostics and an n-gram predictor independently; v1 must have the learned fingerprint adapter contribute to logits and to the training objective.",
    "Quantized signatures define an explicitly quantized observation protocol. They must not be conflated with equality of the unquantized continuous probe values.",
    "Terminal singleton fibres make empirical factorization nearly vacuous; v1 test design must preserve nontrivial fibres and evaluate generalization on held-out domains.",
    "The threshold-derived ultrametric must enforce d(x,x)=0 and define separately whether distinct terminally-indiscernible objects are identified in quotient geometry.",
    "A provided JSONL contains one malformed record at line 784; original is preserved and ingestion will report rather than silently hide parse failures.",
    "Parquet is supplied but pyarrow was not installed in the execution environment; schema and content must be inspected in a runtime with the declared optional dependency."
  ]
